{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"mutating"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"reconcile"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"with"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"remote"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"EntityStore","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux11EntityStoreV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Entity"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"text":"deleting","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"deletedIDs","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Set","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sh"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"UUID","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4UUIDV"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"preserving","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Set","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sh"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"UUID","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4UUIDV"},{"kind":"text","text":">)"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The rows read from storage for the IDs in question. Rows for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"IDs the caller didn’t ask about are simply not here, and their"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"absence means nothing.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"remote"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"IDs storage reports as deleted elsewhere. Removed with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same origin a full reconcile uses, so no deletion is recorded and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"none is echoed back to the store it came from. An ID that "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remote"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"still holds is "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" removed however it is named here: a live row"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is positive evidence, and a tombstone can be stale."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"deletedIDs"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"IDs the caller knows carry unflushed local intent, exactly"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as in the full reconcile. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remote"},{"type":"text","text":" has no authority over them, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"neither does "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deletedIDs"},{"type":"text","text":". This store’s own un-drained "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore\/changes"},{"type":"text","text":" are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"folded in automatically."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"preserving"}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The counterpart to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore\/reconcile(with:preserving:removingMissing:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"partial read — a refresh of the rows a sync tick reported as changed,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rather than of the whole table. Absorbing rows works identically; what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"changes is where deletions come from.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A partial snapshot ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"cannot"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" infer deletion from absence. An ID missing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from it was not deleted, it was not asked for, and treating the two alike","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"would empty the store on the first partial merge. So removal is driven","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"entirely by ","type":"text"},{"code":"deletedIDs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which the caller must have positive evidence","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for — a history tombstone, not an empty result.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Does ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" record changes — this is a hydration operation, for the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reason the full reconcile isn’t one.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore\/reconcile(with:deleting:preserving:)"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore\/reconcile(with:deleting:preserving:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Reconciles this store against a snapshot covering only "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"some"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" of its IDs."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"reconcile"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"with"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"EntityStore","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux11EntityStoreV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<